---
title: Semolina and Nut Halva
servings: 10
course: Dessert
locale: en
difficulty: Hard
---

= Halva =

Preheat the oven to 220°C. Grease and line the base of a #deep 23cm/9" square solid-base cake tin{}.

Lightly cream the @unsalted butter{115%g}(softened) in a bowl. Add the @caster sugar{115%g}, @orange{1}(finely grated rind) and @orange juice{2%tbsp}, @eggs{3}, @semolina{175%g}, @baking powder{2%tsp}, and @ground hazelnuts{115%g}, and beat the ingredients together until smooth.

Turn into the prepared tin and level the surface. Bake for 15 to ~{20%minutes} until just firm and golden. Leave to cool in the tin.

= Finish =

To make the syrup, put the @caster sugar{350%g} in a #small heavy-based saucepan{} with @water{575%ml} and the @cinnamon sticks{2}(halved). Heat gently, stirring, until the sugar has dissolved completely.

Bring to the boil and boil fast, without stirring, for ~{5%minutes}. Measure half the boiling syrup and add the @lemon juice{2%tbsp} and @orange blossom water{4%tbsp} to it. Pour over the halva. Reserve the remainder of the syrup in the pan.

Leave the halva in the tin until the syrup is absorbed then turn it out on to a plate and cut diagonally into diamond-shaped portions. Scatter with the @hazelnuts (unblanched){50%g}(toasted and chopped) and @almonds (blanched){50%g}(toasted and chopped).

Boil the remaining syrup until slightly thickened (but not too much otherwise it will set hard) then pour it over the halva. Scatter the @orange{1}(shredded rind of) over the cake.

= Serve =

Serve with @clotted cream{}(or lightly whipped cream).